{"obs_mudm4g7a_db205282eeb2":{"hookType":"prompt_submit","id":"obs_mudm4g7a_db205282eeb2","origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-23T04:38:19.619Z","channel":"user"},"raw":{"prompt":"A previous agent produced the plan below to accomplish the user's task. Implement the plan in a fresh context. Treat the plan as the source of user intent, re-read files as needed, and carry the work through implementation and verification.\n\n# Restore Thorium Computer Use\n\n## Summary\n\nChatGPT Community 26.917.61114 rejects the Thorium entry added to `browserExtensions`. Its log shows that this aborts Chrome plugin installation. The resulting stale `latest` cache link leaves Thorium’s native messaging manifest pointing to a missing executable, matching the reported connection failure.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add a regression test first and observe it fail: Thorium must appear in browser diagnostics and the Electron browser registry while the upstream `browserExtensions` list remains unchanged.\n- Update the Thorium feature’s staging code to omit the unsupported `browserExtensions` entry and remove that entry if staging is rerun. Update its README to match.\n- Preserve unrelated working-tree changes and the existing enabled feature set. Build from an isolated checkout using the signed stable package.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Run the focused Thorium tests and an official-bundle build with Thorium alone, then inspect the patch report and native package.\n- Install the repaired package and restart ChatGPT Community and Thorium. Confirm the Chrome plugin installs without the schema error, `latest` resolves to the current host with its configuration, the Thorium manifest targets an executable, and Computer Use connects and completes a simple browser action.\n\n## Assumption\n\nThe failed plugin installation caused the stale cache link. Live verification is required before calling the connection fixed.\n"},"sessionId":"01a0cc8e-aec6-7183-9aa5-c96913a8ace1","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:38:19.619Z","userPr