est` made Thorium `sync-manifest.sh` return 1; with `set -Eeuo pipefail` that aborts launch. Append `exit 0` after its deferred retry loop and retain the missing-cache regression test. [Task 4]\n1071:- Skills generally load progressively when selected, while MCP servers can add persistent tool/context overhead. Browser is the in-app browser; Chrome is the external Thorium extension session. [Task 2]\n2445:scope: audit and install the Linux desktop build safely, repair shared app-server or Thorium native-host integration, diagnose Computer Use runtime symptoms, manage local feature acceptance, or route the saved opt-in opportunity-research plan\n2477:- shared-app-server-socket, getConfigOverrides, codex_app, thread/start, MCP, transport: stdio, -c, b95f2f5, git index.lock, make build-app, fetch failed, EPERM\n2479:## Task 6: Fix Thorium native-host manifest installer drift, partial\n2487:- Thorium, native messaging, installManifest.mjs, extension-ids.json, patchManifestInstaller, No compatible Codex app-server entry was found, NativeMessagingHosts, typescript-language-server, Operation not permitted\n2499:## Task 8: Repair Thorium native-host integration against current upstream; package ready, not installed, partial\n2507:- Thorium, native messaging, browserExtensions, browserDiagnostics, installManifest.mjs, .vite/build/src-*.js, extracted-app:pre-webview, native-host manifest, make pacman, 9/9, 43/44, dpkg-deb EPERM\n2551:- when a package is ready and the user says “give me install cmd” -> provide the exact `pacman -U` command directly and mention only the required ChatGPT Community/Thorium restart. [Task 8]\n2564:- `linux-features/shared-app-server-socket/patch.js` must retain upstream `getConfigOverrides` and spawn the shared `app-server` authority with each generated value as repeated `-c <override>` pairs. A bundled-Codex check accepted `codex_app` as `transport: stdio` and completed `thread/start`; focused socket regression coverage passed. [Task 5]\n2566:- Thorium has two independent surfaces: `scripts/extension-ids.json` controls discovery, while `scripts/installManifest.mjs` embeds native-messaging manifest directories. `patchManifestInstaller()` in `linux-features/thorium-chrome-plugin/patch-chrome-plugin.js` idempotently adds `.config/thorium/NativeMessagingHosts` after the Google Chrome-for-Testing anchor. [Task 6]\n2567:- A stale Thorium manifest can yield `No compatible Codex app-server entry was found` even with registry support, because host identity is checked against current `extensionHostPath`. The observed legacy host was cache release `26.803.81509`; current runtime was `26.820.71523`. Tests passed: Thorium feature 6/6, framework 1/1, syntax checks, and `git diff --check`. [Task 6]\n2571:- Current upstream splits Thorium inventory between `browserDiagnostics` and `browserExtensions`; register Thorium in both. The shared Chromium registry now lives in `.vite/build/src-*.js`, so the feature needs an `extracted-app:pre-webview` descriptor. Prelaunch/cold-start hooks regenerate the manifest from the current cache; a stale host path can fail even when discovery is correct. [Task 8]\n2572:- On an isolated detached worktree at `origin/main` `241435e`, Thorium focused tests were 9/9, and `make pacman` produced `/tmp/codex-desktop-linux-repair-ready/dist/codex-desktop-2026.08.30.155556-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst` from a cached hash-verified `chatgpt 26.825.51511` package. The official packaged-manifest checker returned `correct: true`, mode 600, current host, and both extension origins. [Task 8]\n2574:- Validate package identity/layout, launcher `--diagnose`, shell syntax, patched Electron `node --check`, upstream hash/provenance, and absence of upstream `/usr`/`/etc` payload paths. The resulting package was not installed; live ChatGPT Community/Thorium bridge proof remains pending. [Task 9]\n2586:- Symptom: resolved upstream-pull files remain `UU`, or `make build-app` ends in `fetch failed`. Cause: the sandbox could no