air_thorium_native_host_manifest_current_upstream.md (cwd=/home/chris/04_Src/codex-desktop-linux, rollout_path=/home/chris/.codex/sessions/2026/08/30/rollout-2026-08-30T11-13-05-01a0533b-38cd-7db1-b048-f585034f7833.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-31T13:04:26+00:00, thread_id=01a0533b-38cd-7db1-b048-f585034f7833, partial; current-upstream package and isolated hook QA passed, installation/restart pending)\n\n### keywords\n\n- Thorium, native messaging, browserExtensions, browserDiagnostics, installManifest.mjs, .vite/build/src-*.js, extracted-app:pre-webview, native-host manifest, make pacman, 9/9, 43/44, dpkg-deb EPERM\n\n## Task 9: Safely pull current upstream-equivalent revision and rebuild a feature-preserving Arch package, partial\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-03T16-59-07-Wmn7-isolated_pull_rebuild_codex_desktop_linux.md (cwd=/home/chris/04_Src/codex-desktop-linux, rollout_path=/home/chris/.codex/sessions/2026/09/03/rollout-2026-09-03T12-59-07-01a06835-bea1-70e1-84bd-b4b934cae7d1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-03T17:15:08+00:00, thread_id=01a06835-bea1-70e1-84bd-b4b934cae7d1, partial; isolated package build passed; package not installed/restarted)\n\n### keywords\n- The GUI updater rebuilds from frozen `/opt/codex-desktop/update-builder`; after fixing this checkout, an authorized recovery is `make install-native`, not Check for Updates. The fixed source was not installed/restarted in this rollout. [Task 4]\n- On CachyOS/Niri/Wayland, the bundled Computer Use backend is the correct path; doctor checks AT-SPI, Niri window control, portal input/screenshots, `/dev/uinput`, and development input. Backend/plugin registration is separate from UI visibility: use `CODEX_LINUX_ENABLE_COMPUTER_USE_UI=1` for a one-build UI opt-in. [Task 1]\n- `enabled-feature-drift` is a descriptor/config mismatch, not a bypass condition. The 27-feature attempt became accepted-with-warnings/zero blockers only after removing the eight drifted ids and rerunning direct `scripts/validate-upstream-dmg.js --enforce`; 19 features remained enabled. [Task 1]\n- After `make install-native`, compare running app/webview/plugin start times to package install time, inspect stale hashed-asset errors, fully terminate old processes, then restart. `Failed to fetch dynamically imported module` here came from an old Electron renderer after `/opt/codex-desktop` replacement, not missing Computer Use payload; post-restart cache/install SHA and doctor matched. [Task 1]\n- `linux-features/shared-app-server-socket/patch.js` must retain upstream `getConfigOverrides` and spawn the shared `app-server` authority with each generated value as repeated `-c <override>` pairs. A bundled-Codex check accepted `codex_app` as `transport: stdio` and completed `thread/start`; focused socket regression coverage passed. [Task 5]\n- Upstream `main` was fast-forwarded from `6bd3816` to `b95f2f5` while tracked local work was retained in `stash@{0}: On main: codex-pull-preserve-20260827`. Conflict intent was upstream’s current Computer Use descriptor architecture plus the local shared-socket override regression and upstream Unix-socket path helper. [Task 5]\n- Thorium has two independent surfaces: `scripts/extension-ids.json` controls discovery, while `scripts/installManifest.mjs` embeds native-messaging manifest directories. `patchManifestInstaller()` in `linux-features/thorium-chrome-plugin/patch-chrome-plugin.js` idempotently adds `.config/thorium/NativeMessagingHosts` after the Google Chrome-for-Testing anchor. [Task 6]\n- A stale Thorium manifest can yield `No compatible Codex app-server entry was found` even with registry support, because host identity is checked against current `extensionHostPath`. The observed legacy host was cache release `26.803.81509`; current runtime was `26.820.71523`. Tests passed: Thorium feature 6/6, framework 1/1, syntax checks, and `git diff --check`. [Task 6]\n- For signed package `26.820.71523`, stale feature patches fail critical drift checks: use current `origin/main` (`b95f2f5`) in a detached worktree and run `node --test scripts/lib/linux-features.test.js linux-features/*/test.js`. The validated native package had 31 user-facing features, 69 applied patches, 762 pass/0 fail, and `pacman -Qkk` found 0 altered files. `directory-only-working-tree-watch` conflicts with `shallow-repository-watches`; omit internal Nix-only `nix-store-bundled-marketplace-permissions` from native packages. [Task 7]\n- `launcher/start.sh.template` must export `CODEX_HOME`, `CODEX_LINUX_APP_DIR`, `CODEX_LINUX_APP_STATE_DIR`, `CODEX_LINUX_FEATURES_DIR`, and `CODEX_LINUX_LAUNCHER_LOG`; prelaunch/cold-start hooks receive app/state/cache-log paths, and after-exit additionally receives Electron exit status. Prove the contract with `launcher provides the documented runtime hook contract`, `node --test launcher/start.test.js` (8/8), and `bash tests/scripts_smoke.sh`. [Task 7]\n- Verify installed state through `/opt/codex-desktop/resources/codex-linux-build-info.json`, patch report, `/opt/codex-desktop/start.sh --diagnose`, and Computer Use doctor. Read Aloud can use native `spd-say`/`espeak-ng` when Kokoro assets are absent. [Task 7]\n- Current upstream splits Thorium inventory between `browserDiagnostics` and `browserExtensions`; register Thorium in both. The shared Chromium registry now lives in `.vite/build/src-*.js`, so the feature needs an `extracted-app:pre-webview` descriptor. Prelaunch/cold-start hooks regenerate the manifest from the current cache; a stale host path can fail even when discovery is correct. [Task 8]\n- On an isolated detached worktree at `origin/main` `241435e`, Thorium focused tests were 9/9, and `make pacman` produced `/tmp/codex-desktop-linux-repair-ready/dist/codex-desktop-2026.08.30.155556-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst` from a cached hash-verified `chatgpt 26.825.51511` package. The official packaged-manifest checker returned `correct: true`, mode 600, current host, and both extension origins. [Task 8]\n- If the original checkout is dirty/conflicted or `.git` is read-only, use `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/main`, create a clean detached clone/worktree at that SHA, and preserve ignored `linux-features/features.json` from the original so enabled features/settings are retained. The validated isolated build used `aac6178`, cached hash-verified `chatgpt 26.901.20858`, and preserved 29 enabled feature IDs. [Task 9]\n- Validate package identity/layout, launcher `--diagnose`, shell syntax, patched Electron `node --check`, upstream hash/provenance, and absence of upstream `/usr`/`/etc` payload paths. The resulting package was not installed; live ChatGPT Community/Thorium bridge proof remains pending. [Task 9]\n- At the observed state, `main` was `0ee586f`, ahead 1/behind 16 with `MERGE_HEAD=aac6178`, four unresolved files, staged/untracked work, and read-only `.git/FETCH_HEAD`. Preserve it; use a writable, network-enabled shell for fetch/pull. Public main was `23c55eb`, so cached `aac6178` cannot be claimed current. [Task 10]\n"},"sessionId":"01a0cc8e-aec6-7183-9aa5-c96913a8ace1","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:38:33.698Z","toolInput":{"command":"sed -n '2495,2515p' /home/chris/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md; sed -n '2560,2575p' /home/chris/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"},"toolName":"Bash","toolOutput":"### keywords\n\n- make install-native, linux-features/features.json, compatibility.json, b95f2f5, 26.820.71523, 762 pass, spawnSync bash EPERM, launcher/start.sh.template, CODEX_LINUX_FEATURES_DIR, cold-start hook, pacman -Qkk, start.sh --diagnose\n\n## Task 8: Repair Thorium native-host integration against current upstream; package ready, not installed, partial\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-30T15-13-05-L2qD-repair_thorium_native_host_manifest_current_upstream.md (cwd=/home/chris/04_Src/codex-desktop-linux, rollout_path=/home/chris/.codex/sessions/2026/08/30/rollout-2026-08-30T11-13-05-01a0533b-38cd-7db1-b048-f585034f7833.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-31T13:04:26+00:00